Priority: 1
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: improve-selection-hit-geometry, add-marquee-selection, add-multi-select

Goal:
Change box selection so objects are selected only when the selection box fully contains them, instead of selecting on partial overlap.

Context:
The user explicitly asked for selection behavior to change from partial-touch selection to full-overlap selection for shapes and strokes. This is a selection-policy change on top of the existing marquee system.

Expected changes:

- update marquee selection rules from intersection-based inclusion to full containment
- define how freehand strokes are treated under containment, using their real geometry or a justified approximation
- keep additive marquee behavior consistent with the new containment rule

Acceptance criteria:

- Dragging a marquee across only part of a shape or stroke does not select it.
- Dragging a marquee that fully contains a shape or stroke does select it.
- Multi-select and additive marquee behavior still work with the new containment rule.
- The rule is consistent enough that the user can predict what will and will not be selected.

Notes:

- This task is about marquee or drag-box selection policy, not click hit testing.
- If stroke containment needs a tolerance margin, keep it explicit and small.
